{
  "id": "serial-correlation",
  "term": "serial correlation",
  "definition": "Serial correlation is the tendency for repeated measurements from the same person to be related to one another across time rather than acting like independent observations. In N-of-1 data, failing to account for this time-linked pattern can lead simple statistical tests to give misleading results.",
