      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports serial correlation in repeated observations from an individual, but it does not explicitly define it as a time-linked pattern or as measurements that are related “across time.”",
        "The claim that failing to account for it makes simple statistical tests give “misleading results” is an unsupported generalization beyond the packet’s wording, which only says usual/simple methods do not account for serial correlation and that accounting for it can change inferences."
